course: dictionary
lesson: 8061
title: Words that connect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word related is a useful one. It has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The two questions are related.» Here related means connected in some way, so the two questions share a link.
explain: «We are related — she is my cousin.» Here related means in the same family. A cousin is part of your family, so the clue is cousin.
explain: Related can also be the past form of the verb relate, which means to tell a story or to understand someone's feelings. When you see related, ask yourself: is it describing things that connect, people in one family, or a word that shows something happened in the past? The sentence will guide you.
fact: Related means connected in some way, or in the same family.
fact: Related is the past form of the verb relate: relate, relates, related, relating.
fact: Useful phrases include «related to», «closely related» and «related facts».
fact: In maths, 3 + 4 = 7 and 7 − 4 = 3 are related facts, because they use the same three numbers.
fact: «Tenrecs look like hedgehogs or shrews but are actually related to elephants and aardvarks.»
exercise: «The two questions are related.» What does related mean here? | Angry with each other | *Connected in some way | Written in pencil | Two of the same colour
exercise: «3 + 4 = 7 and 7 − 4 = 3 are ___ facts.» Which word fits the gap? | Ancient | Barely | Glum | *Related
exercise: «She is my cousin, so we are ___.» Which word means in the same family? | *Related | Curt | Famished | Glum
test: In «Tenrecs look like hedgehogs or shrews but are actually related to elephants and aardvarks», what does related mean? | *Connected, closely linked by family | Hidden under the ground | Hungry for food | Painted in bright colours
test: Which sentence uses related to mean in the same family? | The path was treacherous. | *We are related, she is my cousin. | The dog's tail drooped. | The children were famished.
exam: Which is the past form of the verb relate? | relates | *related | relation | relating
